@namespace NSail.Components

@* What a menu says rather than offers: who you are at its top, the version at its foot. It
   is not an item — no click, no tab stop — and it is presentational to the list it renders
   inside, so a menu never offers an option that does nothing. The rule that separates it from
   the items is drawn by position (ns-mud.css), not written here: a block that opens the menu
   is ruled underneath and one that closes it is ruled above, so neither end needs a divider
   the caller has to remember. *@
<div class="ns-menu-block" role="presentation">
    @ChildContent
</div>

@code {

    [Parameter]
    public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
